{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","type":"heading","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"type":"text","text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" generates that class for you (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<StructName>Observer"},{"text":") and wires up the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers take "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". They never "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", never "},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and never call I\/O directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void"},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs effects in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so they don’t block UI. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"4. Persistence is invisible","anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" properties; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" records every change in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"reference"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" debounces and drains those changesets through ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You never write ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code."}]},{"text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","type":"heading","anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","type":"heading","anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two structural patterns:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decision rule: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does this need to know your action type?"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs use "},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to read from the store and dispatch on "},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those plugins are blind to it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","type":"heading","anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@concurrent"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","type":"heading","anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux gives you a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppEnvironment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A network layer (use ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and Swidux doesn’t care).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading","anchor":"Anti-patterns"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"try","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from inside a reducer — use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Owning the store with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"ObservableObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Buffering form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Registering ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" before ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — snapshot must precede mutation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Design Principles","roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Explanation","anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"title":"ChangeSet","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"title":"Plugin Architecture","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"title":"Effect","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect."}],"title":"Send","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"title":"UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}],"title":"Build Your First Swidux App","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"title":"Architecture & Performance","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work."}],"title":"StateWriter","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"}}}